---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { release, launch, launchLabel, dateLabel, sourceUrl, site } from '../../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Releases" description={`Latest public stable release: ${release.latest.tag}, ${dateLabel(release.latest.date)}. Real release notes, history and validation caveats.`}>
  <div class="container"><header class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Releases / Sources and history</span><h1>Know what you’re running.</h1><p class="lead">This site is prepared for v{launch.version}. The latest published stable release is {release.latest.tag}, dated {dateLabel(release.latest.date)}.</p></header>
    <section id="launch-baseline" class="launch-baseline prose"><h2>{launchLabel}</h2>{launch.state === 'candidate' ? <p>The product pages and handbook describe cumulative code at <a href={sourceUrl('CHANGELOG.md')}><code>{launch.commit.slice(0, 8)}</code></a>, the public <code>{launch.ref}</code> checkpoint. It includes the v0.19 and v0.20 stabilization work plus the integrated queue and Copy Actions refinements. It is not a published v0.20 release.</p> : <p>The handbook and technical references are pinned to the verified published v{launch.version} tag.</p>}<p>Reactive Horizon first-run onboarding still needs final integration and verification. The current Setup guide describes only the controls present at this source checkpoint. Physical-terminal acceptance and the final tag are launch gates, not claims made by this website build.</p><p>Homebrew currently provides {release.tapVersion}. <a href="/install/">Installation instructions</a> distinguish the tap from the exact candidate source build. <a href="/docs/reference/changelog/">Read the canonical candidate changelog →</a></p></section>
    <div class="article-layout">
      <aside class="release-index" aria-label="Public release history">{release.history.map(item => <a href={`/releases/${item.tag}/`}><span>{item.tag}</span><small>{item.date}</small></a>)}<a href={`${site.repo}/releases`}>All GitHub releases <span>↗</span></a></aside>
      <article class="prose">
        <div class="release-heading"><h2>{release.latest.tag}</h2><span class="badge">Latest published stable</span></div>
        <p>Published {dateLabel(release.latest.date)}. The original release notes below include the actual changes and their recorded compatibility limits. Candidate code is documented separately from this public history.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button" href={`/releases/${release.latest.tag}/`}>Full release notes <span>→</span></a><a href={release.latest.url}>GitHub release ↗</a></div>
        <h2>Sources you can check</h2><p>Version, date and historical notes come from a checked-in GitHub release snapshot, verified {release.verifiedAt}. The handbook uses the independently pinned launch source. Normal builds work offline; refreshing either source is an explicit review step.</p>
        <p><a href={sourceUrl('CHANGELOG.md')}>Candidate changelog ↗</a> · <a href="/roadmap/">Roadmap and proposals →</a></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
